  for people with no money and here we are  it's in the middle of summer  um if i can just share this with you  that in 2020  that if 50 pounds of energy  would have lasted you between 10 and 12  days  when the price cap comes in on the 1st  of october that's going to last you  three and a half days  and currently when the price cap goes up  again  on the 1st of january that 50 pounds of  energy is going to last you  2.8 days and that's providing the cap  doesn't go up anymore  it's not certain all these estimates  that we give i think we're getting  reasonably accurate now with the october  cap which will be around 3600 i do  believe that  but we are not sure about the price cap  in  december because we're still referencing  the tariff  and the the price cap tariff reference  period doesn't end until the middle of  november there is plenty of there's  plenty of opportunity for putin to cause  us more trouble squeeze gas and see  prices go even higher that's why we've  got to take action sorry i interrupted  you no no just say that that  the chancellor and business uh  and energy companies are meeting  tomorrow um  any hope that this will be  you know this is obviously something  that that will be on their radar any any  hope that this will be what will come  from that well we started this  conversation about this generic term  energy companies and i mentioned uh that  we are the energy retailers yes we are  an energy company but we are making we  are not profitable as such at present  there are other energy companies there  are people that of course who build wind  farms who have have received subsidies  for renewable schemes there are the oil  majors who are obviously drilling and  for  gas  and those are the companies that are in  at that meeting tomorrow so um  utilita is not at that meeting um  they will have heard today about what  some of us are asking for i hope it gets  discussed but i cannot see that being  concluded we do have several discussions  with government and with the regulator  and i for my part i will continue  my call for a social tariff  excuse me we're hearing about a cost of  living package as well being being put  together  again this is not going to be something  that that either of the uh prospective  tory leaders are going to be held to do  you have any confidence at all that will  make a difference  um  no i'm very concerned  and i think that the the government has  a duty of care  despite its current um situation with  the uh with the outgoing prime minister  but that shouldn't stop them getting  together and deciding and setting a  direction of travel so much ground work  needs to be done in anything that we do  and the sooner we start  with the groundworks of making sure we  can do what we think we can what i'm  saying we can do it needs that ignition  to that plan and that surely  can be given by trust sunac and boris  johnson  are you surprised that you the chairman  of a utility company find yourself in in  a position where you are essentially  trying to come up with social policy  to try to ease poverty for people  does it surprise me yes it does um i but  i have as you when you introduce me i  was the uh  government's chairman of the fuel  poverty advisory group for nearly seven  years and that's exactly what we were  trying to do and we did discuss a social  tariff back then but not in the heat of  the battle or the size of the issue that  we have today  and that's what annoys me even more that  um whilst we had the debates in the past  where the problems were nowhere near as  challenging as they are now i'm not  hearing it enough today with the sense  of urgency it needs because there's  going to be an interregnum as far as um  the the the government is concerned with  the um voting going on for our new  leader they need to give you  the government gets the the level of  concern and the impact that it is having  on people  i think some of them do i thought that  rishi sunak on talk tv last night  um has certainly got what we've been  trying to tell him for a long time so  he's caught up  this needs to be tightly targeted and  very deep to the poor that need it the  most  so um  to me it's palpably obvious what we need  to be doing and enough of us have got to  go and kick the backsides of those that  can do it and the sooner they do it then  i shall start resting a bit easier and i  hope more importantly so so with our  customers a third of our customers a  third of our customer base are on our  priority services register which means  that they have vulnerability issues of  some kind and i've listened into calls  to to hear of their plight and it is  heartbreaking and i come back this is  the summer  not the winter demand in the winter will  go through the roof and it'll be about  they'll be spending about 150 to 160  more this winter than they were last  winter so this is absolutely horrifying  where we're going where we're heading  for  okay derek licorice chairman of utilita  energy good to talk to you today thank  you thank you

